Ion Endoluminal System Instruments and Accessories
PN 553990-11
Rev C
Model IF1000
Publication Date 2024-08
Software PlanPoint OS1 v4.0.0
Software Ion OS1 v6.0.0
Manufacturer Intuitive
Indications for Use
The Ion Endoluminal System is indicated for diagnostic bronchoscopy procedures.
Intended Use
The system assists physicians in accessing peripheral lung lesions.
Intended User
Use by trained interventional pulmonologists.
Intended Patient Population
Adults requiring lung biopsy.
Contraindications
Do not use in patients unable to tolerate bronchoscopy.
Adverse Events
Pneumothorax, bleeding, airway irritation.
Warnings
WARNING: Ensure the catheter is locked before articulating.
WARNING: Confirm imaging registration prior to biopsy.
WARNING: Maintain sterile technique at all times.
WARNING: Keep fiber bundle away from laser sources.
WARNING: Disconnect power before servicing components.
WARNING: Inspect cables for damage before each case.
WARNING: Do not use device if expiration date has passed.
WARNING: Avoid contact with conductive fluids during operation.
WARNING: Maintain airflow to prevent overheating.
WARNING: Secure patient to avoid displacement of catheter.
WARNING: Follow institutional protocols for anesthesia.
Caution
CAUTION: Allow system to warm to operating temperature.
CAUTION: Verify software versions before use.
CAUTION: Avoid pinch points when docking the arm.
CAUTION: Limit catheter torque to specified range.
CAUTION: Use only accessories listed in this manual.
CAUTION: Deactivate suction prior to catheter removal.
CAUTION: Inspect filters weekly for debris accumulation.
CAUTION: Avoid excessive force on articulating joints.
CAUTION: Store equipment in a dry environment.
Note
Note: Status indicators are displayed on the front panel LEDs.
Note: Refer to online resources for training videos.
Note: Record serial numbers for traceability.
Note: Follow hospital policy for instrument cleaning.
Note: Allow components to dry before packaging.
Table 1 LED Status Indicators
State | LED Color | Action
Ready | Green | Proceed
Fault | Red | Halt procedure
Charging | Amber | Keep connected
